.TH "SOPLOS-GRUB-EDITOR" "1" "2026-11-17" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-grub-editor \- graphical editor for the GRUB boot loader of Soplos Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-grub-editor
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-grub-editor
configures the GRUB2 boot loader of Soplos Linux from a graphical interface.
Built with Tauri 2, Rust, and Svelte, it has three views:
.IP \[bu] 2
.B General:
the default boot entry (a fixed entry, the last installed kernel or the last
booted one), the timeout, the screen resolution, the detection of other
operating systems, the recovery entries, the use of UUIDs, the submenus and the
kernel parameters. These are the settings of
.IR /etc/default/grub .
.IP \[bu]
.B Boot Entries:
the entries of the boot menu. The memtest entries and the entries written to
.I /etc/grub.d/40_custom
can be switched off and on, and deleted; new custom entries are added from the
same view. Kernel and operating system entries are generated from what is
installed and cannot be changed one by one.
.IP \[bu]
.B Appearance:
installing, applying, disabling and removing GRUB themes, a custom background
image with its colors, and the conversion of TrueType or OpenType fonts to
GRUB's PF2 format.
.P
The window never runs as root. Every change to the boot files goes through a
single Polkit-gated helper, authenticated with
.BR pkexec (1),
which accepts only a closed list of operations and checks every value before it
writes: a value that could run a command when the file is read by
.BR grub-mkconfig (8)
is refused. Files are replaced whole, never half written, and
.I /etc/default/grub
is checked to be valid shell first. Custom entries are checked with
.BR grub-script-check (1).
.P
Before the first change of a session the program offers to save a copy of
.I /etc/default/grub
where the user chooses. It leaves no backup files of its own.
.P
After a change it offers to run
.BR update-grub (8)
so that it takes effect. On a system that does not boot with GRUB it says so
and changes nothing.
.P
The interface is available in English, Spanish, German, French, Italian,
Portuguese, Romanian and Russian. It starts in the system language and falls
back to English.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show summary of options.
.TP
.B \-\-run-ops \fIFILE\fR
Internal Polkit-authenticated task: validate and run the operations stored in
.IR FILE .
Used by the application itself through
.BR pkexec (1)
and not meant to be called by hand.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
About dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+I
Show or hide the notes.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit the application.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Tab
Next section.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Tab
Previous section.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/grub
The GRUB settings.
.TP
.I /boot/grub/grub.cfg
The generated boot menu, read to list the entries.
.TP
.I /etc/grub.d/40_custom
Custom boot entries written by the program.
.TP
.I /etc/grub.d/20_memtest86+
Memtest entries, which can be switched off and on.
.TP
.I /boot/grub/themes/
Installed GRUB themes.
.TP
.I /boot/grub/fonts/
Installed GRUB fonts.
.TP
.I /boot/grub/custom.cfg
Colors of the custom appearance.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.soplos.grubeditor.policy
Polkit policy defining the administrator privileges for changes to the boot files.
